# Guided desktop tutorial
Workstream-ID: lea-14
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/14
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed desktop option reference and read-only tutorial scope
Status: DONE
Milestone: Explain every desktop control without starting automation or changing private settings
Dependencies: lea-11

## Purpose
Add a replayable in-app walkthrough and a standalone offline tutorial.
Explain per-run customization, persistent configuration, commands, prompts,
real-action boundaries and source-versus-packaged capabilities.

## Tasks
- [x] Trace every desktop control and its actual CLI or persistence behavior.
- [x] Add topic navigation, Back/Next and a contextual per-run settings explanation.
- [x] Provide a standalone tutorial that does not load configuration or initialize history.
- [x] Bundle the public tutorial resource for future Windows builds.
- [x] Update usage documentation and captioned fictional-data screenshots.
- [x] Exercise navigation, replay, errors, keyboard access and state preservation.
- [x] Verify protected native startup and local tutorial delivery.
- [x] Reconcile the reviewed workstream with issue and Project tracking.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] The tutorial covers all five pages and all four per-run settings tabs.
- [x] Navigation never starts commands, sends input, saves editors or creates run presets.
- [x] Opening and closing the tutorial preserves current controls and unsaved edits.
- [x] The standalone entry works without configuration, browser authentication or a database.
- [x] Real submissions/messages, forceful Stop and private preset creation are explained accurately.
- [x] Current source delivery is distinguished from the unchanged published v0.2.0 package.
- [x] Technical verification is not represented as live qualification or human approval.

## Completion evidence
The reviewed guide has 21 topics covering all desktop pages, per-run tabs,
advanced configuration, safety boundaries and first-run steps. A read-only
dialog supports topic selection, Back/Next, replay, toolbar/F1 and contextual
help. Standalone source startup bypasses the normal window, configuration,
database and command runner. An ignored local launcher opens that entry.

Final GUI selection: 118 passing cases and exit zero. Separate tutorial and
window/widget groups passed nine and 31 cases; existing Windows notice tests
passed four cases. Scoped Ruff/Black and product mypy passed, checking 70 source
files. Ten isolated fictional-data captures succeeded, with captioned usage
documentation, contact-sheet inspection and a full tutorial screenshot review.
The font self-test found 287 families and verified Segoe UI rendering.

An initial Windows QSettings isolation error changed native desktop preference
storage and failed four preservation assertions. Explicit default-format /
UserScope constructors fixed isolation. Corrected captures and native checks
preserved the captured post-error preferences and registry timestamp. The
immediately preceding preference was not captured, so no older snapshot was
restored. One corrected 118-case run passed assertions but exited with a Windows
access violation; the separate groups and exact full-selection rerun exited
zero. The cause remains unverified and was not reproduced.

The launcher check and actual protected Windows standalone/normal-window
interactions passed: responsive guide, 21 topics, zero automation children,
normal exit zero and preserved current controls, unsaved edits and original
inputs. Standalone startup did not load private configuration or initialize
history. Temporary qualification state was cleaned.

The Windows entry/spec and smoke source include the guide for future builds.
No new frozen build or release was made; published v0.2.0 is unchanged.
Independent initial API read-back verified exact managed content, one pinned
issue-backed Project item and the persistent backlink. Final settlement
receipts belong in the excluded index/ledger. Source changes remain local and
uncommitted; no live application, invitation or human aesthetic acceptance
is implied.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-08: Scoped a read-only, replayable desktop tutorial. Per-run
  customization changes only selected overrides; Start and Copy command can
  materialize a private preset. Persistent edits remain in Configuration.
  Kept the published package and earlier qualification gaps separate.
- 2026-11-08: Implemented and qualified the read-only source tutorial, contextual
  help and standalone launcher. Documented every exposed option, regenerated
  ten fictional-data previews and aligned the architecture/usage guides.
  Fixed Windows preference isolation, retained the pre-error uncertainty and
  recorded the nonreproduced access-violation exit rather than inventing a cause.
  Existing issue and Project identities were independently verified before
  the scoped completion transition; earlier mappings and review gaps remain.
